# Declining a tsumo by an added kan, then ronning the very same tile (2012 Tenhou shape).
# Seat 0 calls pon on seat 1's 2s and discards 1z, holding 345m 678p 2345s + p222s.
# Waits are 5s (and fifth-copy 2s). Seat 0 draws 5s: tsumo is legal (tanyao, kuitan on).
# Seat 0 declines tsumo by declaring kakan 2s instead (nobody can rob it), draws
# rinshan 7z and tsumogiris it, keeping 345m 678p 3455s + s2222s (still waiting 5s).
# The owed kan dora indicator 2m (dora 3m) is revealed before seat 0's discard on both
# rulesets. Seat 1 then discards 5s before seat 0's next draw: seat 0 is not furiten
# and rons 5s on both rulesets.
# Scoring for Seat 0 (dealer, East):
#   Hand: 345m 678p 345s 55s + s2222s, ron on 5s (tanki).
#   Yaku: tanyao (1) + dora:1 (3m from kan dora indicator 2m; initial 1z -> 2z absent) = 2 han.
#   Fu: 20 base + 8 open simple kan (s2222s) + 2 tanki = 30 fu.
#   Base 30 * 2^(2+2) = 480; dealer ron rounds 6 * 480 = 2880 up to 2900.
#   Dealer repeats East 1 at honba 1.

[meta]
name: declined_tsumo_kakan_ron_same_tile
title: Declining tsumo by added kan leaves no temporary furiten and allows ron on the same tile
rules: both
source: engine.md §4.2, rules.md §4.17, §5.4, §5.13, docs/notes/p3-closeout.md

